    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always felt a natural distance from mathematics, especially compared to subjects like biology or literature. My upper secondary education didn’t foster deep engagement, and despite my parents’ academic backgrounds, I never developed a strong connection. I see math as a structured, often rigid system that doesn’t align with my intuitive, creative thinking. Still, I respect its precision and use it occasionally in practical contexts like budgeting or cooking.",
